# Drupal contribution workspace (Codex)

Read `.drupal-contrib/context.md` in full before contribution work. It contains the shared site table, workflow, and issue-record rules.

Resolve `<skills-root>` to `.agents/skills`. Start with `$drupal-issue-start <url>`.
Explicitly delegate the roles requested by that workflow, using the installed
`.codex/agents/*.toml` definitions. Keep the complete sequential procedure and
site/issue context in each handoff; relay agent pauses to the human.

Use native Codex tools instead of Claude tool names. If a custom role cannot be
selected, give a fresh subagent the corresponding full procedure from
`.drupal-contrib/agents/<name>.md`. If subagents are unavailable, report the
limitation; independent testing must not silently become self-verification.

Trust the project configuration and review/trust the installed hook with `/hooks`
before relying on its Git protection. Resolve `.drupal-contrib/proposals/`
notices first. Do not change global configuration or trust settings automatically.
